  <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">On-policy RL</div><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" data-w="47.2" style="background:var(--green)"><span>0.472</span></div></div></div>
</div>
<p style="font-size:.72rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--ff-mono);text-align:center;margin-top:-.5rem">GSM8K accuracy — bars animate on scroll</p>

<table class="results-table">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Run</th><th>GSM8K</th><th>TruthfulQA</th><th>MMLU</th><th>MMD</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Base</td><td class="mn">0.448</td><td class="mn">0.300</td><td class="mn">0.436</td><td class="mn">—</td><td class="mn">—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mild SFT</td><td class="mn">0.512</td><td class="mn">0.295</td><td class="mn">0.444</td><td class="mn">0.00956</td><td class="mn best">1.001</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Stress SFT (teacher)</td><td class="mn bad">0.420</td><td class="mn bad">0.245</td><td class="mn bad">0.364</td><td class="mn">0.01093</td><td class="mn bad">0.826</td></tr>
    <tr class="highlight-row"><td>OPD ← stress teacher</td><td class="mn">0.466</td><td class="mn">0.275</td><td class="mn">0.430</td><td class="mn">0.01092</td><td class="mn">0.951</td></tr>
    <tr><td>On-policy RL</td><td class="mn">0.472</td><td class="mn">0.290</td><td class="mn">0.442</td><td class="mn">0.01098</td><td class="mn best">0.990</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>The highlighted row is the headline: <strong>OPD beats the degraded teacher it learned from on all three tasks</strong>, despite identical MMD drift to that teacher. Read the table top to bottom and the loss-function vocabulary can't separate stress SFT from OPD — they share the same broken teacher. The state-source view can: one applies supervision off-policy, the other on the learner's own states.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="ct">The takeaway</div>
  <p>Post-training is not only about the form of the loss — maximum likelihood, policy gradient, or KL. It is about <strong>where in the model's state space supervision is applied</strong>. On-policy state supervision preserves locality, lets students improve beyond degraded teachers, and keeps general capabilities intact under target-task pressure. The authors note this is a small-scale, single-GPU study (one base model, LoRA, lexical-feature drift) — evidence for a mechanism, not a benchmark claim.</p>
</div>
</section>

<!-- Listen-friendly content -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: Post-Training is About States, Not Tokens</h2>
    <p>This paper reframes language model post-training. Instead of comparing supervised fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, and distillation by their loss functions, it asks where the supervision is applied. In an autoregressive model every update lands on a state — the prompt plus the generated prefix. SFT trains on fixed dataset states that the model may never visit, while RL and on-policy distillation train on states the learner itself generates.</p>
    <p>Three findings, all on Qwen3-0.6B-Base with GSM8K as the target and TruthfulQA and MMLU as retention tests. First, mild SFT improves the target with almost no forgetting, but stress SFT — five epochs, high learning rate — degrades both retention and the target task itself. Second, on-policy distillation from that degraded teacher surpasses the teacher on every task, because the student queries the teacher locally on its own states rather than copying the teacher's bad trajectories. Third, lightweight on-policy RL improves the target with negligible forgetting. Strikingly, all three methods produce nearly identical scalar rollout drift, yet forgetting differs by an order of magnitude — proof that distance moved is not the whole story; what matters is which states received supervision.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：后训练关乎状态，而非词元</h2>
    <p>这篇论文重新审视了语言模型的后训练。它不再用损失函数来比较监督微调、强化学习和蒸馏，而是追问监督被施加在哪里。在自回归模型中，每一次更新都落在一个状态上——即提示加上已生成的前缀。监督微调在固定的数据集状态上训练，而模型可能从不访问这些状态；强化学习和在线策略蒸馏则在学习者自己生成的状态上训练。</p>
    <p>论文在 Qwen3-0.6B-Base 上得到三个发现，目标任务是 GSM8K，保持能力用 TruthfulQA 和 MMLU 衡量。第一，温和的微调几乎不遗忘地提升目标任务，但高压微调会同时损害保持能力和目标任务本身。第二，从这个退化教师做在线策略蒸馏的学生，在所有任务上都超过了教师，因为学生是在自己的状态上局部询问教师，而非复制教师的糟糕轨迹。第三，轻量的在线策略强化学习几乎不遗忘地提升目标任务。值得注意的是,这三种方法产生几乎相同的标量漂移，但遗忘程度相差一个数量级——这证明移动的距离不是全部，关键在于哪些状态接受了监督。</p>
  </div>
</div>

</article>

